{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments ["<b>Into which water comes — it becomes impure.</b> Scripture did not impose impurity upon kinds of foods and liquids and seeds until they are prepared for eating, and the application of water is the beginning of their preparation, and their essential significance is for eating. <b>And any liquid.</b> Can I include all liquids? I include strawberry juice and pomegranate juice and all other kinds of fruit juices. Scripture says <b>water</b> — just as water is distinct in that it has no borrowed name, so too I include dew, wine, oil, blood, honey, and milk, which have no borrowed name; and I exclude strawberry juice and pomegranate juice and all other fruit juices, which have a borrowed name." "<b>In any vessel.</b> Just as a vessel is distinct in that it is detached, so too I include that which is detached from the ground, and I exclude that which is in cisterns, pools, and caves, which are not detached."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:32.538862217Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}